<title>USA: UPS driver killed in Tennessee accident.</title>
<headline>UPS driver killed in Tennessee accident.</headline>
<dateline>NASHVILLE, Tenn. 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>A United Parcel Service driver was killed on Monday when his truck toppled off a freeway ramp in Nashville and fell onto busy Interstate 65.</p>
<p>The 18-wheel semi-trailer was attempting to enter the freeway but failed to make a turn on the ramp, police said.</p>
<p>The company said the man who died was a long-time UPS driver-trainer who was substituting for a regular driver because of the Teamsters strike against the company.</p>
<p>The truck was destroyed and packages were strewn across the major north-south highway, blocking traffic.</p>
</text>
